concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "272 4  Meaning of sexual intercourse"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-272-5 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In this Code, sexual intercourse means:  (a) the penetration, to any extent, of the vagina or anus of a person by any part of the body of another person; or  (b) the penetration, to any extent, of the vagina or anus of a person, by an object, carried out by another person; or  (c) fellatio; or  (d) cunnilingus; or  (e) the continuation of any activity mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d).  (2) In this Code, sexual intercourse does not include an act of penetration that:  (a) is carried out for a proper medical or hygienic purpose; or  (b) is carried out for a proper law enforcement purpose.  (3) For the purposes of this section, vagina includes:  (a) any part of a female person’s genitalia; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children" ;
    skos:definition "(1) In this Code, sexual intercourse means:  (a) the penetration, to any extent, of the vagina or anus of a person by any part of the body of another person; or  (b) the penetration, to any extent, of the vagina or anus of a person, by an object, carried out by another person; or  (c) fellatio; or  (d) cunnilingus; or  (e) the continuation of any activity mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d).  (2) In this Code, sexual intercourse does not include an act of penetration that:  (a) is carried out for a proper medical or hygienic purpose; or  (b) is carried out for a proper law enforcement purpose.  (3) For the purposes of this section, vagina includes:  (a) any part of a female person’s genitalia; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "99cc95a88529b61f1ff5d02e73a7b19b98936be3ed2f6850f44155c80effab7a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
