concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-13 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "272 12  Sexual intercourse with young person outside Australia—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-272-13 ;
    values:originalText "defendant in position of trust or authority Engaging in sexual intercourse with young person  (1) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1  (a) the person engages in sexual intercourse with another person (the young person); and  (b) the young person is at least 16 but under 18; and  (c) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (d) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years. Causing young person to engage in sexual intercourse in presence of defendant  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct in relation to another person (the young person); and  (b) that conduct causes the young person to engage in sexual intercourse in the presence of the person; and  (c) the young person is at least 16 but under 18 when the sexual intercourse is engaged in; and  (d) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (e) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) The fault element for paragraph (2)(b) is intention.  (4) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(b) and (d) and (2)(c) and (e). Note 1: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Note 2: For a defence based on belief about age, see section 272.16.  (5) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(c) and (2)(d). Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1." ;
    skos:definition "defendant in position of trust or authority Engaging in sexual intercourse with young person  (1) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1  (a) the person engages in sexual intercourse with another person (the young person); and  (b) the young person is at least 16 but under 18; and  (c) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (d) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years. Causing young person to engage in sexual intercourse in presence of defendant  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct in relation to another person (the young person); and  (b) that conduct causes the young person to engage in sexual intercourse in the presence of the person; and  (c) the young person is at least 16 but under 18 when the sexual intercourse is engaged in; and  (d) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (e) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) The fault element for paragraph (2)(b) is intention.  (4) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(b) and (d) and (2)(c) and (e). Note 1: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Note 2: For a defence based on belief about age, see section 272.16.  (5) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(c) and (2)(d). Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "396cb4dd6260e6c818ad896b9f14d0ea8d433e606b86da1d8369fe60adac7dad" ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
