    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1  (a) the person engages in sexual intercourse with another person (the young person); and  (b) the young person is at least 16 but under 18; and  (c) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (d) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years. Causing young person to engage in sexual intercourse in presence of defendant" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1  (a) the person engages in sexual intercourse with another person (the young person); and  (b) the young person is at least 16 but under 18; and  (c) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (d) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years. Causing young person to engage in sexual intercourse in presence of defendant"@en ;
