concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "272(2) 12  Sexual intercourse with young person outside Australia—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-272-13-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct in relation to another person (the young person); and  (b) that conduct causes the young person to engage in sexual intercourse in the presence of the person; and  (c) the young person is at least 16 but under 18 when the sexual intercourse is engaged in; and  (d) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (e) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct in relation to another person (the young person); and  (b) that conduct causes the young person to engage in sexual intercourse in the presence of the person; and  (c) the young person is at least 16 but under 18 when the sexual intercourse is engaged in; and  (d) the person is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the young person; and  (e) the sexual intercourse is engaged in outside Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ee60b64d970b6ba361381b8125befc540c5e8b50ce6049fb90d685310e655a56" ;
