concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "272 15  “Grooming” child to engage in sexual activity outside"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-272-16 ;
    values:originalText "Australia  (1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct in relation to another person (the child); and  (b) the person does so with the intention of making it easier to procure the child to engage in sexual activity (whether or not with the person) outside Australia; and  (c) the child is someone:  (i) who is under 16; or  (ii) who the person believes to be under 16; and  (d) one or more of the following apply:  (i) the conduct referred to in paragraph (a) occurs wholly or partly outside Australia;  (ii) the child is outside Australia when the conduct referred to in paragraph (a) occurs;  (iii) the conduct referred to in paragraph (a) occurs wholly in Australia and the child is in Australia when that conduct occurs. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to subparagraph (1)(c)(i) and paragraph (1)(d). Note 1: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Note 2: For a defence based on belief about age, see section 272.16.  (3) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1) even if it is impossible for the sexual activity referred to in that subsection to take place.  (4) For the purposes of subsection (1), it does not matter that the child is a fictitious person represented to the person as a real person. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1" ;
    skos:definition "Australia  (1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct in relation to another person (the child); and  (b) the person does so with the intention of making it easier to procure the child to engage in sexual activity (whether or not with the person) outside Australia; and  (c) the child is someone:  (i) who is under 16; or  (ii) who the person believes to be under 16; and  (d) one or more of the following apply:  (i) the conduct referred to in paragraph (a) occurs wholly or partly outside Australia;  (ii) the child is outside Australia when the conduct referred to in paragraph (a) occurs;  (iii) the conduct referred to in paragraph (a) occurs wholly in Australia and the child is in Australia when that conduct occurs. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to subparagraph (1)(c)(i) and paragraph (1)(d). Note 1: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Note 2: For a defence based on belief about age, see section 272.16.  (3) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1) even if it is impossible for the sexual activity referred to in that subsection to take place.  (4) For the purposes of subsection (1), it does not matter that the child is a fictitious person represented to the person as a real person. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c1ef40ce0484c698eb4bd27fe56c1e7b68d74f9780ed674210d0e5013dae45e9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-16-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-16-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-16-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-16-ss-4 ;
