doc:sch-1-sec-272-19 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "272 8(1), 272.9(1), 272.12(1) or 272.13(1) if the defendant proves" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "that:  (a) at the time of the sexual intercourse or sexual activity, there existed between the defendant and the child or the young person a marriage that was valid, or recognised as valid, under the law of:  (i) the place where the marriage was solemnised; or  (ii) the place where the offence was committed; or  (iii) the place of the defendant’s residence or domicile; and  (b) when it was solemnised, the marriage was genuine. Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see section 13.4. Offences involving procuring or “grooming” child for sexual activity  (2) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against subsection" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "272 14(1) or 272.15(1) if the defendant proves that:"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-272-20 ;
    values:originalText "(a) at the time he or she committed the offence, there existed between the defendant and the child a marriage that was valid, or recognised as valid, under the law of:  (i) the place where the marriage was solemnised; or  (ii) the place where the offence was committed; or  (iii) the place of the defendant’s residence or domicile; and  (b) when it was solemnised, the marriage was genuine. Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see section 13.4. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1  Subdivision C—Offences of benefiting from, encouraging or preparing for sexual offences against children outside Australia" ;
    skos:definition "(a) at the time he or she committed the offence, there existed between the defendant and the child a marriage that was valid, or recognised as valid, under the law of:  (i) the place where the marriage was solemnised; or  (ii) the place where the offence was committed; or  (iii) the place of the defendant’s residence or domicile; and  (b) when it was solemnised, the marriage was genuine. Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see section 13.4. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1  Subdivision C—Offences of benefiting from, encouraging or preparing for sexual offences against children outside Australia"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6630dc93856bd236daed8cb416d04d427e590bcbbf7f7e4d97dc7c97d210a97b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
