doc:sch-1-sec-272-20 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "272 14(1) or 272.15(1) if the defendant proves that:" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(a) at the time he or she committed the offence, there existed between the defendant and the child a marriage that was valid, or recognised as valid, under the law of:  (i) the place where the marriage was solemnised; or  (ii) the place where the offence was committed; or  (iii) the place of the defendant’s residence or domicile; and  (b) when it was solemnised, the marriage was genuine. Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see section 13.4. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences outside Australia  Part 1  Subdivision C—Offences of benefiting from, encouraging or preparing for sexual offences against children outside Australia" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-21 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "272 18  Benefiting from offence against this Division"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-272-21 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the person does so with the intention of benefiting from an offence against this Division; and  (c) the conduct is reasonably capable of resulting in the person benefiting from such an offence. Penalty: Imprisonment for 20 years.  (2) Subsection (1) applies:  (a) whether the conduct is engaged in within or outside Australia; and  (b) whether or not the person intends to benefit financially from an offence against this Division; and  (c) whether or not an offence against this Division is in fact committed.  (3) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(c). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the person does so with the intention of benefiting from an offence against this Division; and  (c) the conduct is reasonably capable of resulting in the person benefiting from such an offence. Penalty: Imprisonment for 20 years.  (2) Subsection (1) applies:  (a) whether the conduct is engaged in within or outside Australia; and  (b) whether or not the person intends to benefit financially from an offence against this Division; and  (c) whether or not an offence against this Division is in fact committed.  (3) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(c). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2ab936346a026a06744812ce494cc9b80acbd5c18fb207dbf9d45c0495af1d05" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-21-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-21-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-272-21-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010.pdf, p.23" .
doc:sch-1-sec-272-21 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "272 18  Benefiting from offence against this Division" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the person does so with the intention of benefiting from an offence against this Division; and  (c) the conduct is reasonably capable of resulting in the person benefiting from such an offence. Penalty: Imprisonment for 20 years.  (2) Subsection (1) applies:  (a) whether the conduct is engaged in within or outside Australia; and  (b) whether or not the person intends to benefit financially from an offence against this Division; and  (c) whether or not an offence against this Division is in fact committed.  (3) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(c). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2." ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer .

