concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-273-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "273 2A  Consent to commencement of proceedings where defendant"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-273-3 ;
    values:originalText "under 18  (1) Proceedings for an offence against this Division must not be commenced without the consent of the Attorney-General if the defendant was under 18 at the time he or she allegedly engaged in the conduct constituting the offence.  (2) However, a person may be arrested for, charged with, or remanded in custody or on bail in connection with, such an offence before the necessary consent has been given." ;
    skos:definition "under 18  (1) Proceedings for an offence against this Division must not be commenced without the consent of the Attorney-General if the defendant was under 18 at the time he or she allegedly engaged in the conduct constituting the offence.  (2) However, a person may be arrested for, charged with, or remanded in custody or on bail in connection with, such an offence before the necessary consent has been given."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1da6c501bac672e4e8e4850e8bdfc97cc82a69afa1322102cb0b28869971e926" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
