doc:sch-1-sec-471-6-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "471(2) 21  Defences in respect of child abuse material" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), conduct is of public benefit if, and only if, the conduct is necessary for or of assistance in:  (a) enforcing a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences involving postal or similar services, or carriage services  Part 2  (b) monitoring compliance with, or investigating a contravention of, a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or  (c) the administration of justice; or  (d) conducting scientific, medical or educational research that has been approved by the Minister in writing for the purposes of this section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-471-6-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "471(3) 21  Defences in respect of child abuse material"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-471-6-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against section 471.19 (using a postal or similar service for child abuse material) or 471.20 (possessing etc. child abuse material for use through a postal or similar service) if:  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3)." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against section 471.19 (using a postal or similar service for child abuse material) or 471.20 (possessing etc. child abuse material for use through a postal or similar service) if:  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6ac149310e9298227ae3d3b011feefaedb919498dc688c6dd6a631e3c4bab6b2" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-471-6 ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defendant bears evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
