    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person (the defendant) commits an offence if:  (a) the defendant engages in conduct in relation to another person (the child); and  (b) that conduct causes the child to engage in sexual activity with another person (the participant) using a carriage service; and  (c) the child is under 16 years of age when the sexual activity is engaged in; and  (d) the participant is at least 18 years of age when the sexual activity is engaged in. Penalty: Imprisonment for 15 years." ;
