concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-53 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "53 After subsection 474.28(7) of the Criminal Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-53 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: Issues relating to aggravated offence involving sexual activity  (7A) For the purposes of an offence against subsection 474.25B(1):  (a) there is no fault element for the physical element described in paragraph (a) of that subsection other than the fault elements (however described), if any, for the underlying offence; and  (b) absolute liability applies to the physical element of circumstance of the offence that the child has a mental impairment; and  (c) strict liability applies to the physical element of circumstance of the offence that the defendant is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the child, or the child is otherwise under the care, supervision or authority of the defendant. Note 1: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Note 2: For strict liability, see section 6.1. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children" ;
    skos:definition "Insert: Issues relating to aggravated offence involving sexual activity  (7A) For the purposes of an offence against subsection 474.25B(1):  (a) there is no fault element for the physical element described in paragraph (a) of that subsection other than the fault elements (however described), if any, for the underlying offence; and  (b) absolute liability applies to the physical element of circumstance of the offence that the child has a mental impairment; and  (c) strict liability applies to the physical element of circumstance of the offence that the defendant is in a position of trust or authority in relation to the child, or the child is otherwise under the care, supervision or authority of the defendant. Note 1: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Note 2: For strict liability, see section 6.1. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "05857b079384c8ec23cd44f3a3660b52de6fad8f852bf614d6d7622010bcef53" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No fault element for physical element of circumstance that child has a mental impairment or defendant is in a position of trust or authority." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010.pdf, p.59" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-53-norm .
