concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-474-13 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "474 29  Defences to offences against this Subdivision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-474-13 ;
    values:originalText "Offences involving sexual activity—belief that child at least 16 years of age  (1) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against section 474.25A if the defendant proves that, at the time the sexual activity was engaged in, he or she believed that the child was at least 16 years of age. Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see section 13.4. Offences involving sexual activity with other participant—belief that participant under 18 years of age  (2) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against subsection" ;
    skos:definition "Offences involving sexual activity—belief that child at least 16 years of age  (1) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against section 474.25A if the defendant proves that, at the time the sexual activity was engaged in, he or she believed that the child was at least 16 years of age. Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see section 13.4. Offences involving sexual activity with other participant—belief that participant under 18 years of age  (2) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against subsection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1c0a3e792c48e037b81fbe045ad6ec45f38d56df7448a386398e6df6210144f7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
