    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "defendant committed the offence, he or she believed that the child did not have a mental impairment. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Amendments relating to sexual offences against children  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to child sex offences involving postal or similar services, or carriage services  Part 2  Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see section 13.4. Offences involving procuring or “grooming” person for sexual activity with other participant—belief that participant under 18 years of age  (4) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against subsection" ;
