concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-475 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "475 1A  Defences for NRS employees and emergency call persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-475 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of Subdivision C, D, E, F or G of Division 474 in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an employee of an NRS provider; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an employee.  (2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of Subdivision C, D, E, F or G of Division 474 in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an emergency call person; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an emergency call person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of Subdivision C, D, E, F or G of Division 474 in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an employee of an NRS provider; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an employee.  (2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of Subdivision C, D, E, F or G of Division 474 in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an emergency call person; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an emergency call person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "91058683c1abd5198ec740adcb4b7af4f2ff4b2edc19c7b0ed1c29dc8e4416b2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-475-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-1-sec-475-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
