doc:sch-2-sec-23zb-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23ZB(3) Forfeiture of material by operation of law" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The forfeiture notice is a notice that:  (a) identifies the forfeitable thing; and  (b) states the constable’s belief that the thing is derived from, or was used in connection with, the commission of a Commonwealth child sex offence; and  (c) states that the thing will be forfeited to the Commonwealth 30 days after the notice is given, unless any of the following persons object to the forfeiture by written notice given before ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Forfeiture of child sex material  Schedule 2  the end of that period to the head of the police force that includes the constable:  (i) a person who owns the thing (either alone or with other persons);  (ii) a person who has a right to possess the thing; and  (d) explains the circumstances in which, under section 23ZC, a person may be given a copy of parts of the thing, or of data contained in the thing, on request to the head of the police force made within 30 days after the notice is given; and  (e) explains the effect of forfeiture of the thing; and  (f) explains the circumstances in which compensation is payable in connection with forfeiture of the thing; and  (g) requests a person claiming compensation for forfeiture of the thing to notify the head of the police force of the claim. Giving copy of forfeiture notice to others affected" ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-2-sec-23zb-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23ZB(4) Forfeiture of material by operation of law"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23zb-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the constable gives the forfeiture notice to a person described in subsection (2), the constable may also give a copy of the notice to anyone whom the constable reasonably believes will be directly or indirectly affected by the proposed forfeiture of the forfeitable thing. Effect of giving forfeiture notice" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the constable gives the forfeiture notice to a person described in subsection (2), the constable may also give a copy of the notice to anyone whom the constable reasonably believes will be directly or indirectly affected by the proposed forfeiture of the forfeitable thing. Effect of giving forfeiture notice"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c392ac10f06cbc41f844c505c4d136469e71d1ae2a2d915a01610ed8ea0e4f70" ;
