doc:sch-2-sec-23zb-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23ZB(6) Forfeiture of material by operation of law" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) If there is an objection described in paragraph (3)(c) but the head of the police force that includes the constable considers that the forfeitable thing should be forfeited to the Commonwealth despite the objection:  (a) the head of the police force must instruct the Director of Public Prosecutions to apply for an order under section 23ZD for the forfeiture of the thing; and  (b) the Director must make the application. Objection or lack of one does not affect prosecution" ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-2-sec-23zb-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23ZB(7) Forfeiture of material by operation of law"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23zb-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) Evidence of the fact that a person described in paragraph (3)(c) objected or did not object as described in that paragraph is not ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Schedule 2  Forfeiture of child sex material  68            Crimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Offences Against Children) Act 2010       No. 42, 2010 admissible against the person in a prosecution of the person for a Commonwealth child sex offence." ;
    skos:definition "(7) Evidence of the fact that a person described in paragraph (3)(c) objected or did not object as described in that paragraph is not ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Schedule 2  Forfeiture of child sex material  68            Crimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Offences Against Children) Act 2010       No. 42, 2010 admissible against the person in a prosecution of the person for a Commonwealth child sex offence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "89c426f079d72a1a1c28bed87f1fa192161dd50e3e22ab166d48bfddd5eb09a7" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-2-sec-23zb ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Evidence of non-objecting is not admissible in a prosecution for a Commonwealth child sex offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
