    cml:logicSummary "Part IE of the Crimes Act 1914 applies to Commonwealth child sex offences." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-9 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9 Application of Part IE of the Crimes Act 1914" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Part IE of the Crimes Act 1914 applies in relation to Commonwealth child sex offences, whether the conduct constituting the offences occurred before, on or after the commencement of that Part. (2) Part IE of the Crimes Act 1914 also applies in relation to the following offences constituted by conduct that occurred before the commencement of that Part as if they were Commonwealth child sex offences:  (a) an offence against former Part IIIA of the Crimes Act 1914 (which was about child sex tourism);  (b) an offence against section 474.19, 474.20, 474.22, 474.23," ;
    cof:pageNumber "76"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-sexual-offences-against-children-act-2010-sch-2-sec-474 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "474 26 or 474.27 of the Criminal Code as in force before the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-474 ;
    values:originalText "commencement of Schedule 1 to this Act;  (c) an offence against section 11.1, 11.4 or 11.5 of the Criminal Code relating to an offence described in paragraph (a) or (b) of this subitem;  (d) an offence against a provision described in paragraph (a) or (b) of this subitem taken to have been committed because of section 11.2, 11.2A or 11.3 of the Criminal Code; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Forfeiture of child sex material  Schedule 2  (e) an offence against former Part IIIA of the Crimes Act 1914 taken to have been committed because of former section 5 of that Act;  (f) an offence against former section 7, 7A or 86 of the Crimes Act 1914 relating to an offence against former Part IIIA of that Act.  [Minister’s second reading speech made in— House of Representatives on 4 February 2010 Senate on 10 March 2010]  (20/10) ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042" ;
    skos:definition "commencement of Schedule 1 to this Act;  (c) an offence against section 11.1, 11.4 or 11.5 of the Criminal Code relating to an offence described in paragraph (a) or (b) of this subitem;  (d) an offence against a provision described in paragraph (a) or (b) of this subitem taken to have been committed because of section 11.2, 11.2A or 11.3 of the Criminal Code; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042  Forfeiture of child sex material  Schedule 2  (e) an offence against former Part IIIA of the Crimes Act 1914 taken to have been committed because of former section 5 of that Act;  (f) an offence against former section 7, 7A or 86 of the Crimes Act 1914 relating to an offence against former Part IIIA of that Act.  [Minister’s second reading speech made in— House of Representatives on 4 February 2010 Senate on 10 March 2010]  (20/10) ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00042"@en ;
